#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544913} :activity/id #uuid "4fe3e7fe-66b2-56e4-b07b-e2a8d0dd2aac" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048986 :topic/id #uuid "d11c4451-1bcb-5f1a-a6d3-3f5fdbe85bb7" :topic/math-academy-id 1997} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544906 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83af4c85-31c8-5333-8b0c-d044a02bd3da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267303} {:answer/id #uuid "8835a210-9de5-5c5f-a9a0-4264ee64fa8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267345} {:answer/id #uuid "bda7f1f6-caae-5b5a-912d-ad3b965431f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{x+1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267847} {:answer/id #uuid "c79e2d71-f72b-5349-9f02-4326a7a438da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267934} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9ca14f-93c5-5b93-88bb-be41c8973bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267970}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267934} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfe90643-e048-5d75-985f-e9ed17b022bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "88491dc6-a6a9-5e2a-ab57-c63ec8866fd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-132574" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}-1}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/92/926e4c717707d13fdb9562e149d2f41c3ab657b42fbae35c0953019ab93a06b6.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-{y}^{2}-1\\le x\\le -y\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](images/89/8933233e8aca4a36ee90ffec69ca6e93d0523d3fa50c400d2cdea78f9ec80812.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=\\sqrt{-x-1}\\,$ and $\\,y=1.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=-x.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le -1,\\,\\sqrt{-x-1}\\le y\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le -x\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}-1}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{-x-1}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "19c28e52-fdaf-5ad1-b61f-5be844edc12c"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544913 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129652 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1158bf19-5d87-5d3c-ae18-4b6a90a7b40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(1+{e}^{-4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544121} {:answer/id #uuid "3290e5fa-709a-5cf8-9205-a80c7e9bb0ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(1-{e}^{-4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544199} {:answer/id #uuid "8d52f326-a07f-5846-9198-2281c9cb0ce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544391} {:answer/id #uuid "fc472a25-8431-51bb-a98c-291448f6d760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544638} {:answer/id #uuid "fd3e3379-5ac5-5f47-9142-c0dd3eb25756" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}(1+e)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544640}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544199} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ae90e2c-9b42-50f3-a4dd-8cea89d355b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c1b66dc5-759e-5b16-9d35-fc67c34a4499" :question/math-academy-id "q-38466" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/79/79326f0f463d3b26db4ab497045fa35aa5aa7fb68be6fd79b5ebd633a4d6646f.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y\\,⟹\\,y=x,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. Its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/44/4452d48cac6bd387e8f7f27a9aedfbe51f9c5e478a5288f889aa3378c4805d34.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}[y]_{0}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-{x}^{2}}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-{e}^{-4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2ea8c9b7-08dd-5aab-ac0c-8a662422b3d5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544963}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544914 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351412 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32fbf319-3234-58a8-95fb-c53b859ed56b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{16}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348902} {:answer/id #uuid "49820777-b895-52a8-9251-7d27144fa1b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}(1-{e}^{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349114} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6fed8a-5620-59e2-bea5-d6cea14b66c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349455} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe1cda9-fe65-5b36-99c7-49ccecf2e000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349473} {:answer/id #uuid "f9126db6-0a47-59b1-b887-454248d2f098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-{e}^{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350634}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349473} :answer-field/id #uuid "a55be9a3-3b8c-5e73-9f00-cfe58e1d5da1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0524dddc-0711-51cc-bea5-211d12fb3f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-82296" :question/problem "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d5/d5d777577f85cd577ce35bfd3a99c1e2218622d1856f4fe7ee4afe1cfd2c9f86.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 8,\\,\\sqrt[3]{y}\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt[3]{y}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. Its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05ec37a8f4fd33c05a2438df5c5fbc697f8b560fde0b9fe73922a0db56a09c2c.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{4}}[y]_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,{e}^{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{{x}^{4}}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{16}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2ef3a076-a0cb-5e87-9202-566dbdfa7430" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544964}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544963 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad97339-5570-5d24-b1fb-77ec680fac1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2-y}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544142} {:answer/id #uuid "55f54e57-e18b-5d0c-9c19-13b3bfe26010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544276} {:answer/id #uuid "6a97f4e4-20e0-58ad-87bc-d933151f4bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544319} {:answer/id #uuid "bcca3de2-d84e-525d-b4d1-8d4e8c0a5627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}{\\int }_{2-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544487} {:answer/id #uuid "c31f4f8b-4dd6-5e15-bb60-2549b490b990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544503}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544319} :answer-field/id #uuid "d330fe8c-c0b4-581d-86c1-4285baf2910e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "437b2f48-85ba-532a-9ac5-52a828cb51ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-82254" :question/problem "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/47/472aa6b0afe20f7c1902446102265f758637c9ec00eb985bf38a658dc92f3fe5.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type I regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}\\}\\,\\cup \\,\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2-x\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=2-x\\,⟹\\,x=2-y.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\sqrt[3]{y}\\le x\\le 2-y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/77/77b59ce5c40514338b0d23a31e7028c7fa0f7343aad018576301fcc4ec441ac1.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt[3]{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b59367e0-e2c1-5b73-8886-7978e62c8aa2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544914}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544964 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d78785e-c462-55f8-9982-52dc361d2a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{1-y}}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\sqrt[3]{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544150} {:answer/id #uuid "3160ccd4-b4fb-549a-a695-6ba7523ae759" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544196} {:answer/id #uuid "bce3792a-58d1-5db4-971f-0dd4799c18a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-y}}^{\\sqrt[3]{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544489} {:answer/id #uuid "d96c9ebe-385a-5aa9-8cce-0af1acc3fe17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544554} {:answer/id #uuid "e027944a-9ba9-531c-961b-bd1358b11e5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544571}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544554} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad3fdbb4-05c4-5223-8593-ecad3e3ec912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c3ba9c34-ab2d-5d40-bb57-ca2ed5ef7608" :question/math-academy-id "q-82347" :question/problem "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}-1}^{1-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/ab/abf9e5dda9e98caac491aa5d94b3e2ae3f08f90d6bd490762adabc1437ac49d9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}-1\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](images/a4/a45e4b63b1eff23617abcbe33ce522652b20de6c817dfde2d9cdda52d12bb778.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt[3]{y+1}.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt{1-y}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y+1}\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{1-y}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}-1}^{1-{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b6285502-e482-59e6-94a7-bdde0989b515" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544906}}] :activity/title "Changing the Order of Integration in Double Integrals" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544075}]}
